// MOVIE_GUIDANCE: per-movie content guidance for "Check a worry" and the
// Pre-Show card on Tonight's pick, keyed by movie `num` (as a string).
//
// Written once at catalog-update time from each movie's own `full` notes and
// `flags`, never from anything else. Nothing here runs a model in the
// browser and nothing leaves the device.
//
// Shape of each entry:
//   concerns: exactly these 5 keys
//     parentInDanger, scaryVillain, sadOrLoss (death, grief, loss),
//     rudeHumor, animalPeril
//     each { level: "yes" | "mild" | "no", quote }
//     - quote is copied word for word from that movie's `full` text
//     - "no" means the notes don't mention it (not a guarantee), quote ""
//   preShow: an OpenUI Lang 1.0 program for the built-in openuiChatLibrary
//     of @openuidev/browser-bundle@0.2.1 (published 2026-10-15). A Card
//     with a header, up to 3 tags from `flags`, a warning Callout only when
//     the notes describe a moment worth prepping for, and one "Ask after"
//     question as plain TextContent (not a clickable follow-up). Gentle
//     films get a one-line card instead.
//
// `node scripts/validate-guidance.mjs` (also run by validate-data.mjs) checks
// every movie has an entry, every quote is verbatim, and every preShow parses.
// Bundled into data-bundle.js like the other data files.

